      "options": [
        "$q^2 + p + 14 = 0$",
        "$q^2 - 4p - 12 = 0$",
        "$p^2 - 4q - 12 = 0$",
        "$p^2 - 4q + 12 = 0$"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "$p^2 - 4q - 12 = 0$",
      "positiveMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "hint": "",
      "explanation": "",
      "media": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_1786910793821_6pflzf",
      "text": "If $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are distinct roots of $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$ where $a, b, c$ are non-zero real numbers, then $\\frac{a\\alpha^2 + b\\alpha + 6c}{a\\beta^2 + b\\beta + 9c} + \\frac{a\\beta^2 + b\\beta + 19c}{a\\alpha^2 + b\\alpha + 13c}$ is equal to:",
      "type": "mcq",
      "options": [
        "$18c$",
        "$27c$",
        "$\\frac{36}{27}$",
