      "text": "The graph of $y = ax^2 + bx + c$ is given such that $a < 0$, $b > 0$, $c > 0$, and roots are $\\alpha < 0 < \\beta$ with $|\\alpha| < \\beta$. Which of the following is (are) correct?\ni) $ab^3c^3 < 0$\nii) $ab < 0$\niii) $bc(4a + 2b + c) > 0$\niv) $ab(4a - 2b + c) > 0$\nv) $b^2 > 4(a^2 + ac)$\nvi) $ax^2 + bx + c > 0 \\quad \\forall x \\in (\\alpha, \\beta)$",
